 * a circle with a round hook, and the 9 is the same shape turned half a turn.
 *
 * Every glyph holds the same number of evenly spaced points, with sharp corners kept exactly, and the stroke direction
 * of each is chosen so that neighbouring digits line up. That lets any digit be blended into another point by point:
 * the line itself travels from one shape to the next, instead of one number fading out and another fading in.
 *
 * The table is generated: each digit is built from arcs and lines in a 0.62 x 1 box, resampled to [N] points by arc
 * length, then oriented to minimise the travel between 0-1, 1-2 ... 8-9, 9-0 and the other changes a clock makes.
